    "narrative": "Our strongest plays today center on **Cal Raleigh** (73.69) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (69.42), both of whom are projected for high-efficiency outings due to favorable park factors and high-leverage lineup slots. **Cal Raleigh** remains a premier start against Jump, as his +10% park factor and the dynamic platoon advantage provide a massive ceiling for power production. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** occupies the #2 hole, and despite a moderate SP skill rating from Prielipp, his consistent recency and lineup protection make him the anchor of our infield production. **Bryce Harper** (64.39) rounds out the elite tier; despite facing a capable arm in Mahle, his projected xwOBA of 0.389 and the boost from batting third signal a high-floor game for our slugger.\n\nRegarding the bench, the decision to sit **Dylan Beavers** (49.13) was the most difficult. While his elite speed would typically provide a boost in our scarcity-driven strategy, his projected efficiency fell just short of the starters, largely due to a difficult matchup against Miles. Conversely, **Kyle Karros** (63.11) earned the UTIL spot over other bench candidates because of a significant +19% boost from the SP skill matchup against Sears, effectively overriding the raw base projections of other depth pieces. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Yainer Diaz** (41.37) and **Zack Gelof** (46.61); both sit near the lower bounds of our start threshold due to significant negative adjustments for SP skill and park factors, respectively. We will monitor for any late-breaking lineup changes that might impact these margins, but as it stands, our roster is optimized to prioritize the high-efficiency platoon advantages identified in the ATC data.",
